<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Local on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/local/</link><description>Recent content in Local on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 02 Jun 2014 05:52:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/local/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Macedonian Cyrillic</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/116973/</link><pubDate>Mon, 02 Jun 2014 05:52:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/116973/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m making a sans serif with Bulgarian and Serbian glyphs available via locl feature. I&amp;rsquo;ve got a question here: since Macedonian before 1945 was considered a Bulgarian dialect, should it use Bulgarian glyphs? Or it is closer to Serbian?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Typeseeing</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/114158/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Feb 2014 04:53:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/114158/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hello,&lt;br&gt;
my name is Krzysztof Stryjewski and I am graphic design student from Poland and I would like to tell you about my master&amp;rsquo;s project - typeseeing.&lt;br&gt;
Typeseeing is meant to be a guide, collecting voices and thoughts on local typography from different parts of the world. If I receive enough answers, this small anthology will be published and everyone whose text is included in the book will receive a copy.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Alaska</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/34499/</link><pubDate>Fri, 15 Jun 2007 16:45:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/34499/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150415104941/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Indices"&gt;Indices&lt;/a&gt; : &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150415104941/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Geography"&gt;Geography&lt;/a&gt; : &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150415104941/http:/typophile.com/wiki/United%20States"&gt;United States&lt;/a&gt; : Alaska&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
